"bc6b7572-6525-5f0a-acdf-da49eecac498" :question/math-academy-id "q-330498" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-2,4)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨0,3,-5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨1,-2,4⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨0,3,-5⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ & =⟨1,-2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ & =-26 \\\\ 3y-5z & =-26 \\\\ 3y-5z+26 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330498/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34272b7-a7ad-5a58-974e-54cca957d06e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330498"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127964/selection/80ced888585b652cf20a0089117763b4f2a2af417e0b6ef6db87074746080a91" :answer/id #uuid "897a956c-d023-565a-89e6-f1c1dec226a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3y+2z-7=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127964/selection/a9308336d367d2eb05055f0279cbeb80da6213d6b798a58b227fc0133e8a7031" :answer/id #uuid "d48859ef-c554-5111-a8cb-ebfe1415602d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-2y+z-13=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127964/selection/82d25848643c2d70e7cbcd8cdd0abd52dc993cb19aefd6ac69d3e347cf70fe95" :answer/id #uuid "53a79750-d4cb-5287-aa29-e0ad549c69c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-3y+z-17=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127964/selection/4eca69a53e12c15f878ef4935455e10e2178dc8c4b657f70951a99f04abf482a" :answer/id #uuid "ecf4c908-9846-58e4-945d-de793e39c0de" :answ