b235282bd639b42" "q-127971/selection/98d52028a1e32a12e1c0d94494084f114cbf0fd024be3b98e39418cfaa46b10a" "q-127971/selection/a64a2b5e5272666e2941295e4fa9dcf392afbef8b6a117a853c5a6a2674887eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127971" :question/id #uuid "b0724766-b916-5512-ba7c-b23eb1b74775" :question/math-academy-id "q-127971" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-2,1,-3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨-2,7,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-2,1,-3⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨-2,7,-1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ & =⟨-2,1,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ & =14 \\\\ -2x+7y-z & =14 \\\\ -2x+7y-z-14 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127971/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34272b7-a7ad-5a58-974e-54cca957d06e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127971"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127967/selection/83783f1d2117571b03834fa71506db056e686eeff4bd8f9dea200506651fe804" :answer/id #uuid "cfd52b89-44ba-5ac6-aa3e-ee8390f035fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-4y-z+9=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127967/selection/418b5e910b58dbb96a7b392074935d489617808ec49e583f94cbd91a23f2affe" :answer/id #uuid "8fad3f9f-dd27-58db-96a2-20d9a9edd43f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+4y-z-7=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127967/selection/2b940cf1c35f6b15cdb81aa07a60b2f8baa0f8f99b6d4c8ed497240a687a2e88" :answer/id #uuid "9660022