he vector $⟨5,0,-3⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨5,0,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,0,-3⟩ & =⟨3,-2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨5,0,-3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,0,-3⟩ & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨5,0,-3⟩ & =12 \\\\ 5x-3z & =12 \\\\ 5x-3z-12 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336538/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2173739c-cd59-58ed-a265-8ee88c982ae0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336538"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128375/selection/082ef89869106675a46063e5b0f5a00d74468837e4d283ceee7fb4d18063ca37" :answer/id #uuid "cd99359a-d1c3-5457-b5b6-6118cb4ec749" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x+7y-10=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128375/selection/9cede22c1de360b13c46e187709b604cdc99b2a6410bafd5bb4adcfb72a53b73" :answer/id #uuid "40e26e1c-d4ed-58d5-9242-ce5a467ee39c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x+7z+20=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128375/selection/74840b14cf12f8dbad731b195a5e02a5156d25d1ac5ef9847920ca5e41e1248a" :answer/id #uuid "41b312ce-a5c6-513e-b632-bac4c864b0aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x+7z+5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128375/selection/3952c1353438c07d99e852915a27fd9870debdedc370e649ee2479ddb7350d11" :answer/id #uuid "311a1aac-dbb2-538c-b650-99bb37bef703" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2y+7z+10=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128375/selection/5b90d671eb22e3836e9be836b2b4fe0947d186085c799ca1c276f5c15f10768a" :answer/id #uuid "cef1874f-6ea3-57d7-afc7-3ffd29c4bde0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7x+7y+7z-20=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128375/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27f77d74-147d-58b0-9a6b-e200b5888d6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128375/selection/9cede22c1de360b13c46e187709b604cdc99b2a6410bafd5bb4adcfb72a53b73" :answer-field/choices ["q-128375/selection/082ef89869106675a46063e5b0f5a00d74468837e4d283ceee7fb4d18063ca37" "q-128375/selection/9cede22c1de360b13c46e187709b604cdc99b2a6410bafd5bb4adcfb72a53b73" "q-128375/selection/74840b14cf12f8dbad731b195a5e02a5156d25d1ac5ef9847920ca5e41e1248a" "q-128375/selection/3952c1353438c07d99e852915a27fd9870debdedc370e649ee2479ddb7350d11" "q-128375/selection/5b90d671eb22e3836e9be836b2b4fe0947d186085c799ca1c276f5c15f10768a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128375" :question/id #uuid "1d90c80a-6e49-52b9-8044-4809ca79d408" :question/math-academy-id "q-128375" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,0,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=7-2t \\\\ y=7 \\\\ z=7t\\end{aligned}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,0,-2⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨-2,0,7⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨-2,0,7⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ & =⟨3,0,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ & =-20 \\\\ -2x+7z & =-20 \\\\ -2x+7z+20 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128375/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2173739c-cd59-58ed-a265-8ee88c982ae0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128375"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33923"] :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $x-y+4z+16=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨1,-1,4⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+4z+16 & =0 \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{4}x+\\frac{1}{4}y-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-4.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-4)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-4⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-4⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-128380/selection/937c84e3a84ad11269884927d5e7ea19b1d6e9495668338a48a2b4c56077b605" :answer/id #uuid "7c11b77b-6e9b-500f-a0e8-cc24d11fa912" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨-4,4,-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128380/selection/ce5dfac28d3fa9b499824c6a9f4700e2274cd6f9225abc76efef319dcb8f4966" :answer/id #uuid "a190fab2-2f20-5523-a7aa-681ffd89d3e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,2⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128380/selection/d9045543386f7d628df6bc8bdf5999f539b2c49cedc1051de6b65a3f06cfe52c" :answer/id #uuid "ad939636-b869-5138-9191-4d02b30ce1d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,-2,4⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128380/selection/60a63c0f3d25fe56d8a4cec3d78fec838b3d50dc1c4f583e580e0caa5cf023e0" :answer/id #uuid "5f0aba5a-fa9a-5bb1-887a-0103271ca435" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128380/selection/2422d92388cb8f94c19b199a01599dc9467ddb4942740ba7bc8c0678952ad179" :answer/id #uuid "bb8e7568-047d-5e41-b63c-205aaff1af1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,4,-4⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128380/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c922b201-a92f-5395-b5f0-4c722b17bf84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128380/selection/60a63c0f3d25fe56d8a4cec3d78fec838b3d50dc1c4f583e580e0caa5cf023e0" :answer-field/choices ["q-128380/selection/937c84e3a84ad11269884927d5e7ea19b1d6e9495668338a48a2b4c56077b605" "q-128380/selection/ce5dfac28d3fa9b499824c6a9f4700e2274cd6f9225abc76efef319dcb8f4966" "q-128380/selection/d9045543386f7d628df6bc8bdf5999f539b2c49cedc1051de6b65a3f06cfe52c" "q-128380/selection/60a63c0f3d25fe56d8a4cec3d78fec838b3d50dc1c4f583e580e0caa5cf023e0" "q-128380/selection/2422d92388cb8f94c19b199a01599dc9467ddb4942740ba7bc8c0678952ad179"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128380" :question/id #uuid "8cbb9ba9-50e9-5a94-a501-7a9ce40ae41e" :question/math-academy-id "q-128380" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $4x+4y-2z=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨4,4,-2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+4y-2z & =0 \\\\ 2z & =4x+4y \\\\ z & =2x+2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=0.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128380/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128380"] :db/ensure [:kno